meta {
  name: Get Order Forbidden
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/order/{{orderId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{secondUserAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Requires order-service/Create Order.bru (order owned by the FIRST test user, needs
  {{orderId}}) and this folder's Register Second User.bru + Login Second User.bru
  (needs {{secondUserAccessToken}}) to have all run first.

  A different, authenticated, non-admin user tries to read someone else's order by id.

  Expected: 403 FORBIDDEN — OrderAccessDeniedException, via ProblemDetail
  (GlobalExceptionHandler.handleAccessDenied). Contrast with the FraudShield sibling
  project's ledger-service/account-service, which return 403 the same way for
  cross-user access — but note transaction-service's Get Transaction there has NO such
  check, while order-service's Get Order DOES (findById checks ownership on every call,
  not just at creation).
}
